#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Synthetic dispatch tests for researchctld direct C/D and delegated A/B.

``dispatch()`` is exercised with in-memory fakes for ResearchDB,
AuthorityStore and daemon_context, so:
  * no production daemon is started (no Server/Handler/Unix socket);
  * no production (or any) database is opened -- the apsw stub from the
    harness fails loudly on any accidental connection, and the fakes record
    that no research.sqlite file is ever created.

The tests pin the current v3 wiring:
  * direct C/D routes to AuthorityStore.register_amendment_direct with the
    ctx built from (peer_pid, peer_uid) and a daemon-side fail-closed guard
    for missing/non-string/non-empty fields;
  * delegated A/B routes to AuthorityStore.register_amendment;
  * C/D on the delegated wire is passed through and rejected by the store
    (ROOT_CANNOT_REGISTER_C_OR_D) -- CLI choices are the parser-level gate;
  * the v3 schema gate runs before any authority command and fails closed
    when schema_version() reports a non-v3 database.
"""

